Code Defence Intelligence Brief
Date: Tuesday, November 10, 2026
Series: Vol. 2, No. 300
Today's threat intelligence landscape for Tuesday, November 10, 2026 is headlined by Google releasing emergency security updates for the eighth Chrome zero-day flaw of the year (CVE-2026-125350) actively exploited in wild attacks, Barracuda Networks warning that threat actors are actively exploiting critical Email Security Gateway (ESG) code injection vulnerabilities (CVE-2026-116779) for unauthenticated root access, and ESET/BleepingComputer reports exposing Russian state-sponsored threat group Turla deploying a novel "Cereal" malware toolset to spy on government Microsoft Exchange servers.
Strategic Highlights
 * Google Patches Eighth Chrome Zero-Day (CVE-2026-125350) Exploited in Wild Attacks: Official security bulletins from @Google and BleepingComputer confirm emergency desktop updates resolving a critical use-after-free vulnerability in XML parsing subroutines. Remote unauthenticated attackers transmit malformed web content to trigger memory corruption and achieve arbitrary remote code execution across Linux, Windows, and macOS endpoints.
 * Active Wild Exploitation Hits Barracuda ESG Flaws for Unauthenticated Root Access (CVE-2026-116779): Advisories from @Barracuda, @CISA, and SecurityWeek confirm attackers are actively weaponizing code injection flaw CVE-2026-116779. Remote unauthenticated actors submit crafted email attachments to execute arbitrary commands with root privileges and plant persistent backdoors.
 * Turla APT Group Deploys New "Cereal" Malware to Spy on Government Microsoft Exchange Servers: Cyber threat intelligence reports from @Microsoft Threat Intelligence and BleepingComputer detail a campaign targeting European government mail servers. Russian threat group Turla installs custom IIS web modules and transport agents to intercept mail store items and exfiltrate diplomatic correspondence.
 * LinkedIn Tags: Web browser developers, email gateway vendors, operating system maintainers, and federal regulatory bodies managed by @Google, @Barracuda, @Microsoft, and @CISA are natively cross-referenced using assigned LinkedIn URN parameters.
